 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Try a room with thick walls, like a bedroom with the doors closed. If that doesn't work, a large classroom or gym is the most echoic. Try standing in the kitchen with your hands on your hips. Does that make sound louder or quieter? Then buy soundproofing blankets and set up behind one. They' not expensive and they work wonders. Put them around mic rather than at one end of the room. Two blankets each side are often quieter than one on a wall. Also turn off any other sources of noise, like central heating or background music.",
